Description: enable vertical synchronisation
 SDL2 does not set the swap interval by itself, so the intro could render
 as fast as possible depending on the driver. Ask for V-Sync right after
 the OpenGL context creation. The timing of the intro is based on
 SDL_GetTicks(), so the playback speed does not change.
Author: Nicolas HOUDELOT <nicolas@demosdebs.org>
Assisted-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Forwarded: not-needed
Last-Update: 2026-11-14
--- a/src/intro.cpp
+++ b/src/intro.cpp
@@ -609,6 +609,7 @@
   SDL_Window *window = dnload_SDL_CreateWindow("Ghosts of Mars by Faemiyah", 0, 0, static_cast<int>(screen_w),
       static_cast<int>(screen_h), SDL_WINDOW_OPENGL | SDL_WINDOW_RESIZABLE | (flag_fullscreen ? SDL_WINDOW_FULLSCREEN_DESKTOP : 0));
   dnload_SDL_GL_CreateContext(window);
+  SDL_GL_SetSwapInterval(1);
   dnload_SDL_ShowCursor(flag_developer);
 #if defined(USE_LD)
